From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gustavo Belo <gustavobelo28@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 01 Sep 2026 17:36:29 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] rdr2: do not force -vulkan when PROTON_FSR2_UPGRADE is set

The gamefix appends -fullscreen -vulkan unconditionally, and that
argument overrides the renderer chosen in system.xml. PROTON_FSR2_UPGRADE
translates the game's FSR2 calls to FSR4 through amdxcffx64, which is the
DX12 FidelityFX provider and has no Vulkan equivalent, so forcing Vulkan
made the option a silent no-op: the shim would see the game's
ffx_fsr2_api_vk_x64 backend, refuse the context, and leave the game with
no upscaler at all.

Keep -fullscreen, which is what the launch problem the fix was written
for actually needed, and leave the renderer to system.xml when the
upgrade is requested.
---
 gamefixes-steam/1174180.py | 15 ++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/gamefixes-steam/1174180.py b/gamefixes-steam/1174180.py
index 37d6b9e..7790519 100755
--- a/gamefixes-steam/1174180.py
+++ b/gamefixes-steam/1174180.py
@@ -1,8 +1,21 @@
 """Game fix for Red Dead Redemption 2"""
 
+import os
+
 from protonfixes import util
 
 
 def main() -> None:
-    """Sometimes game will not launch if -fullscreen -vulkan is not specified"""
+    """Sometimes game will not launch if -fullscreen -vulkan is not specified
+
+    PROTON_FSR2_UPGRADE translates the game's FSR2 calls to FSR4, and that
+    only exists for the DX12 backend, since amdxcffx64 is the DX12 FidelityFX
+    provider. Forcing -vulkan overrides the renderer picked in system.xml, so
+    it would silently turn the option into a no-op; leave the renderer alone
+    when it is set.
+    """
+    if os.environ.get('PROTON_FSR2_UPGRADE', '0') not in {'0', ''}:
+        util.append_argument('-fullscreen')
+        return
+
     util.append_argument('-fullscreen -vulkan')
